{
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/sarif-2.1/schema/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "fullName": "Trivy Vulnerability Scanner",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/aquasecurity/trivy",
          "name": "Trivy",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-85091",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "zlib versions 1.3.1.2 through 1.3.2 contain a heap buffer overflow vul ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "zlib versions 1.3.1.2 through 1.3.2 contain a heap buffer overflow vulnerability in the gz_vacate() function when processing non-blocking gzwrite() operations with stale external buffer pointers. Attackers can trigger the overflow by calling gzprintf() or gzvprintf() after a write stall, causing an unchecked memmove() to write beyond the internal input buffer boundary."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-85091",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-85091\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: zlib\nFixed Version: 1.3.2-r1\nLink: [CVE-2026-85091](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-85091)\nzlib versions 1.3.1.2 through 1.3.2 contain a heap buffer overflow vulnerability in the gz_vacate() function when processing non-blocking gzwrite() operations with stale external buffer pointers. Attackers can trigger the overflow by calling gzprintf() or gzvprintf() after a write stall, causing an unchecked memmove() to write beyond the internal input buffer boundary.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-85091**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|zlib|1.3.2-r1|[CVE-2026-85091](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-85091)|\n\nzlib versions 1.3.1.2 through 1.3.2 contain a heap buffer overflow vulnerability in the gz_vacate() function when processing non-blocking gzwrite() operations with stale external buffer pointers. Attackers can trigger the overflow by calling gzprintf() or gzvprintf() after a write stall, causing an unchecked memmove() to write beyond the internal input buffer boundary."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "version": "0.75.0"
        }
      },
      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "CVE-2026-85091",
          "ruleIndex": 0,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Package: zlib\nInstalled Version: 1.3.2-r0\nVulnerability CVE-2026-85091\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nFixed Version: 1.3.2-r1\nLink: [CVE-2026-85091](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-85091)"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "security-results/trivy-image-backend/backend-image.tar",
                  "uriBaseId": "ROOTPATH"
                },
                "region": {
